# Known-good SHA512 digests for the Debian netinst images this installer
# is built from. build-iso.sh refuses to extract a source image whose
# digest is not listed here.
#
# The build feeds the source image to xorriso, and on arm64 also to fdisk
# and dd at raw byte offsets. Those are C parsers with a long history of
# ISO9660 and partition-table issues, and they run in a container with
# the whole repository bind-mounted writable, so a repackaged installer
# image reaches the source tree rather than being confined to the image.
# Existence was the only check before this file existed.
#
# Provenance of every digest below:
#
#   1. Fetched from Debian's published checksum lists:
#        https://cdimage.debian.org/cdimage/archive/12.10.0/amd64/iso-cd/SHA512SUMS
#        https://cdimage.debian.org/cdimage/archive/12.10.0/arm64/iso-cd/SHA512SUMS
#   2. Verified each list against its detached SHA512SUMS.sign with the
#      Debian CD signing key, fingerprint
#        DF9B9C49 EAA92984 32589D76 DA87E80D 6294BE9B
#        Debian CD signing key <debian-cd@lists.debian.org>
#      obtained from keyring.debian.org.
#   3. Copied the digests verbatim from the signed lists.
#
# To add a newer point release, repeat those three steps. Do not add a
# digest computed from an image you already have on disk: that pins
# whatever you were given and proves nothing.
#
# Format is `<sha512>  <image>`, the same as sha512sum output. Only the
# digest is matched; the filename is a label, because the build receives
# the image at whatever path the caller supplies.

